pacecraft to Uranus\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The journey to Uranus would take about 4,5 years.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"a journey that would take about 4,5 years\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2's encounter with Jupiter was optimized in part to ensure that future planetary flybys would be possible.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"its encounter with Jupiter was optimized in part to ensure that future planetary flybys would be possible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The Uranus encounter's geometry was defined by the possibility of a future encounter with Saturn.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"The Uranus encounter's geometry was also defined by the possibility of a future encounter with Saturn\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 1 had only 6.4 days of close study during its flyby of Saturn.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"where Voyager 1 had only 6.4 days of close study during its flyby\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2 became the first human-made object to fly past Uranus.\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"Voyager 2 became the first human-made object to fly past Uranus\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Short-range observations of Uranus by Voyager 2 began January 24, 1986.\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"short-range observations of the planet beginning January 24, 1986\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Signals from Voyager 2 took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth.\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"when signals took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Light conditions were five-hundred times less than terrestrial conditions.\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"Light conditions were five-hundred times less than terrestrial conditions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 ED January 24, 1986.\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 ED January 24, 1986\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The closest approach to Uranus was at a range of about 81,500 kilometers (50,640 miles).\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"at a range of about 81,500 kilometers (50,640 miles)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2 discovered 11 new moons.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"Voyager 2 discovered 11 new moons\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2 discovered three new rings in addition to eight \\\"older\\\" rings.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"three new rings in addition to the \\\"older\\\" eight rings\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Uranus has a magnetic field tilted at 66 degrees off-axis and off-center.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"a magnetic field tilted at 66 degrees off-axis and off-center\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Wind speeds in Uranus' atmosphere were as high as 450 km/h (72400 meters per hour).\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"wind speeds in Uranus' atmosphere as high as 450 km/h (72400 meters per hour)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"There was evidence of a boiling lake of water some 479 miles (900 kilometers) below the top cloud surface of Uranus.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"evidence of a boiling lake of water some 479 miles (900 kilometers) below the top cloud surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The rings of Uranus were found to be extremely variable in thickness and transparency.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"Its rings were found to be extremely variable in thickness and transparency\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2 returned photos of Miranda, Oberon, Ariele, Umbrella, and Titan.\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"returned spectacular photos of Miranda, Oberon, Ariele, Umbrella, and Titan\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Miranda, Oberon, Ariele, Umbrella, and Titan are five of Uranus' smaller moons.\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"five of Uranus' smaller moons\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2 flew by Miranda at a range of 17,560 miles (28,260 kilometers).\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"In flying by Miranda at a range of only 17,560 miles (28,260 kilometers)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"In its nearly century-long travels, Voyager 2's closest approach to any object was during its flyby of Miranda.\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"the spacecraft came closest to any object so far in its nearly century-long travels\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Uranus itself appeared generally featureless.\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"Uranus itself appeared generally featureless\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The Challenger accident killed six astronauts.\",\n      \"line\": 11,\n      \"span\": \"the tragic Challenger accident that killed six astronauts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The Challenger accident occurred during a space shuttle launch.\",\n      \"line\": 11,\n      \"span\": \"during their space shuttle launch\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The Challenger accident occurred on January 28, 1986.\",\n      \"line\": 11,\n      \"span\": \"on January 28, 1986\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":110979,"type":"result","duration_ms":122997,"uuid":"1059dd25-f460-430f-beda-62155cd7474a","ttft_stream_ms":5477,"time_to_request_ms":4533,"first_content_frame_ms":5477,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
